<title>FRANCE: CSFB changes Michelin to &quot;hold&quot;.</title>
<headline>CSFB changes Michelin to &quot;hold&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>CS First Boston said it had changed its opinion on French tyre group Michelin to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy&quot;.</p>
<p>It said it was concerned that a sharp expansion of working capital requirements in the first half might have led to negative cash flow and very likely lower returns on invested capital.</p>
<p>For the full year 1996, CSFB expects a earnings per share figure of 26.0 francs, rising to 35.7 francs in 1997 and 41.4 francs in 1998.</p>
</text>
